"The old wooden clock on the mantelpiece ticked with a slow, deliberate rhythm, completely out of sync with the frantic energy of the storm outside. Sheets of rain slammed against the bay window, blurring the streetlights into watery smears of yellow and neon green. Inside, the fireplace crackled weakly, fighting off a chill that seemed to seep directly through the floorboards. On the rug, an overgrown tabby cat stretched lazily, entirely unbothered by the thunder that rattled the china in the cupboard, proving that true peace is mostly a matter of choosing what to ignore."